{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>A threshold alone isn't the whole answer</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Once a suggestion is sitting in "needs review," make it genuinely easy to act on, a one-click accept and a one-click reject, with the original suggestion clearly visible. A review queue nobody actually looks at is barely better than no gate at all.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Track the outcome of every reviewed item, not just whether it was accepted or rejected. If reviewers are accepting the vast majority of below-threshold suggestions, the threshold is probably set too conservatively and just adding friction; if they're rejecting a lot of above-threshold ones, it's set too loosely.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Confidence scores from different model versions or providers aren't always calibrated the same way, a 0.8 from one model release doesn't necessarily mean the same real-world accuracy as 0.8 from the next. Re-validate the threshold against actual review outcomes whenever the underlying model changes, don't assume the old cutoff still means what it used to.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

