{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A model's confidence score is a real signal — don't apply every suggestion the same way when the model itself is telling you how sure it is.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Gate auto-apply behind a confidence threshold: high-confidence suggestions apply automatically, low-confidence ones wait for explicit review.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Set the threshold per action based on blast radius, log scores for every auto-applied action, and re-validate the cutoff whenever the underlying model changes.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
